      en: "Magdala (Amba Mariam) is a historic mountain in Ethiopia, the last stronghold of Emperor Tewodros II. Located on a flat-topped amba in the Amhara region, Tewodros built a fortress here. In 1868, British forces besieged it; the emperor committed suicide after defeat. Ruins of the fortress and cannons remain. The site symbolizes Ethiopian resistance. Excavations have yielded weapons and personal items. Magdala is a national monument and tourist destination.",
